# 1. Find the actual path of `shutdown` on this distro
which shutdown
# typically /usr/sbin/shutdown on Ubuntu, /sbin/shutdown on Amazon Linux

# 2. Find your username (the user that'll run the script)
whoami
# typically ubuntu or ec2-user

# 3. Edit a new sudoers drop-in file via visudo (syntax-checks before saving)
sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/shutdown-nopasswd
In the editor, add one line (substitute your username and the path from step 1):


ubuntu ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/shutdown